mt7601u: expose 802.11w support

mac80211 strips the management frame protection ciphers from the suites it
advertises when the driver does not set MFP_CAPABLE, so wpa_supplicant finds no
BIP cipher and WPA3-SAE is unreachable: SAE requires PMF. mac80211 protects the
frames in software, the driver only has to allow it.

Backport of:
  mt7601u: expose 802.11w support
    https://git.kernel.org/linus/53c2cb8df327

Upstream carries this from v4.19 on. The surrounding code is unchanged between
4.4 and 4.18, so this one patch fits every kernel here that builds the driver.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt7601u/init.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt7601u/init.c
@@ -601,6 +601,7 @@ int mt7601u_register_device(struct mt7601u_dev *dev)
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_HT_CCK_RATES);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, AMPDU_AGGREGATION);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_RC_TABLE);
+	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, MFP_CAPABLE);
 	hw->max_rates = 1;
 	hw->max_report_rates = 7;
 	hw->max_rate_tries = 1;
